From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:33:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] iertutil: the rest of Windows.Foundation.Uri, and
 WwwFormUrlDecoder.

The members the parser commit left as stubs, each as a probe measured
them on Windows:

- Equals compares through IUri_IsEqual, so case in the scheme and host,
  a default port, dot segments and escaped unreserved characters do not
  count, and case in the path, query or fragment does.
- CombineUri and CreateWithRelativeUri resolve through
  CoInternetCombineUrlEx; an empty relative URI is E_POINTER.
- Port is S_FALSE and 0 for a scheme with no port of its own.
- Suspicious is set for a host that is not all ASCII.
- AbsoluteCanonicalUri has the host in punycode and everything beyond
  ASCII percent-encoded as UTF-8; DisplayIri keeps both as they are.
  Both decode percent-encoded unreserved characters.
- IStringable reads as AbsoluteUri, and the class names itself.
- IUriEscapeStatics escapes all but unreserved ASCII as UTF-8 and
  unescapes %XX bytes as UTF-8, leaving malformed escapes alone.
- QueryParsed hands the query to a WwwFormUrlDecoder, which is also its
  own activatable class: split at '&' and the first '=', '+' read as a
  space, empty parts kept as entries with no name and no value, and a
  query with anything beyond ASCII giving no entries at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6228e378229495acbee4b7d358d8ac2b37ad9edc)

